//
// Sanity error: Alice names Bob's public key in a block that appears above
// Bob's, so the value does not exist yet where she uses it. The mistake was
// reported as `unknown constant`, "not declared by any principal", which is
// false: Bob declares it eight lines down and even sends it. The same mistake
// written the other way round -- Bob's block first -- already produced the
// right message, so a modeller got a true diagnosis or a false one depending
// only on the order they happened to type the blocks in.
attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	knows private fa
	fx = HASH(fgb)
]

principal Bob[
	knows private fb
	fgb = PUBKEY(fb)
]

Bob -> Alice: fgb

queries[
	confidentiality? fa
]
